<title>PORTUGAL: Bank/Portugal sells marks for escudos - dealers.</title>
<headline>Bank/Portugal sells marks for escudos - dealers.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Portugal intervened on the foreign exchange market on Tuesday, selling marks at around 100.16 escudos, dealers said.  </p>
<p>The escudo was quoted at 100.14/17 at 1341 GMT. The escudo's traded low for the session was 100.17 and the high 99.95.</p>
<p>&quot;The Bank of of Portugal has been selling marks at between 100.16 and 100.17 escudos,&quot; said one trader who asked not to be named.</p>
<p>Central bank officials could not immediately be contacted for comment.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
